1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,270
Ground Truth SQL.

2
00:00:01,950 --> 00:00:04,810
I'm Riya Kapadnis, and this is my final project

3
00:00:04,810 --> 00:00:05,530
pitch.

4
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:09,110
The problem: AI can write database code that

5
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:12,210
runs with no errors, but gives the wrong answer.

6
00:00:12,242 --> 00:00:14,362
Picture an analyst asking an AI:

7
00:00:14,902 --> 00:00:16,342
what is our revenue by country?

8
00:00:16,802 --> 00:00:20,122
The AI writes SQL, the language for asking a

9
00:00:20,122 --> 00:00:21,362
database questions.

10
00:00:21,742 --> 00:00:22,402
It runs.

11
00:00:22,702 --> 00:00:23,642
No errors.

12
00:00:24,102 --> 00:00:26,472
It says the USA made $4,667.

13
00:00:28,102 --> 00:00:30,622
The real answer is $523.

14
00:00:30,867 --> 00:00:33,507
Claude and I drafted that SQL to copy a common

15
00:00:33,507 --> 00:00:36,687
mistake, on a free sample music store database.

16
00:00:37,167 --> 00:00:39,767
One order from Reno, Nevada cost $3.96,

17
00:00:39,767 --> 00:00:41,567
for four songs.

18
00:00:42,227 --> 00:00:44,507
The SQL joined the order to its songs,

19
00:00:44,827 --> 00:00:47,387
so the $3.96 was counted four times.

20
00:00:47,947 --> 00:00:49,527
Do that for every US order,

21
00:00:49,667 --> 00:00:52,247
and the total is almost nine times too high.

22
00:00:52,325 --> 00:00:53,765
It's not the only mistake.

23
00:00:54,325 --> 00:00:55,965
Mix up milliseconds and seconds:

24
00:00:56,050 --> 00:01:00,105
3,500 long songs, not 1,069.

25
00:01:00,705 --> 00:01:02,525
Count purchases, not people:

26
00:01:02,705 --> 00:01:06,725
835 rock buyers, in a store with 59 customers.

27
00:01:07,305 --> 00:01:10,025
Link the wrong columns: no answer at all.

28
00:01:10,125 --> 00:01:11,025
And no errors.

29
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,240
Why does this happen?

30
00:01:12,760 --> 00:01:14,920
People ask data questions in plain English,

31
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:16,860
so most never see the SQL.

32
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:19,500
The AI doesn't know your data.

33
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:21,620
And wrong SQL doesn't crash.

34
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:23,660
It just gives a number people trust.

35
00:01:23,867 --> 00:01:25,827
Other tools don't do this on your data.

36
00:01:26,507 --> 00:01:29,187
BIRD tests AI only on its own databases.

37
00:01:30,047 --> 00:01:32,787
Vanna's built-in answer test looks for words,

38
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:33,967
not right numbers.

39
00:01:34,507 --> 00:01:36,827
On this data, it passed the answer that was nine

40
00:01:36,827 --> 00:01:38,227
times too high.

41
00:01:38,242 --> 00:01:40,622
Ground Truth SQL fills that gap.

42
00:01:41,102 --> 00:01:43,122
Give it your database and questions with checked

43
00:01:43,122 --> 00:01:43,962
answers.

44
00:01:44,462 --> 00:01:47,882
It runs the AI's SQL and the checked SQL,

45
00:01:48,142 --> 00:01:50,702
compares the results, and gives a report card:

46
00:01:51,162 --> 00:01:53,282
what the AI got wrong, and why.

47
00:01:53,325 --> 00:01:54,425
Where will it be used?

48
00:01:54,825 --> 00:01:56,885
Anywhere people ask data questions in plain

49
00:01:56,885 --> 00:01:59,565
English: store sales, finance,

50
00:01:59,645 --> 00:02:02,850
hospitals, marketing, and AI data assistants.

51
00:02:03,445 --> 00:02:05,365
Analysts learn what to double check.

52
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:07,745
Teams test a tool before buying.

53
00:02:08,465 --> 00:02:09,785
Engineers see what to fix.

54
00:02:09,867 --> 00:02:10,747
How does it judge?

55
00:02:11,267 --> 00:02:13,747
By results, not wording, since one answer can be

56
00:02:13,747 --> 00:02:14,807
written many ways.

57
00:02:15,247 --> 00:02:18,147
These two look different, but both give 523.

58
00:02:18,867 --> 00:02:21,747
On 9 test queries, comparing wording judged 6

59
00:02:21,747 --> 00:02:22,367
right.

60
00:02:22,927 --> 00:02:24,747
Comparing results: all 9.

61
00:02:24,825 --> 00:02:27,105
Claude then answered my 8 questions about the

62
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:29,165
music store, three times.

63
00:02:29,605 --> 00:02:31,565
The checker passed 22 of 24.

64
00:02:32,205 --> 00:02:34,485
The two fails were a tie my question never

65
00:02:34,485 --> 00:02:35,145
settled.

66
00:02:35,565 --> 00:02:38,075
Claude wasn't wrong; my question was.

67
00:02:38,075 --> 00:02:40,435
It also caught a mistake in my answer key.

68
00:02:41,015 --> 00:02:43,295
One question asked about 2023,

69
00:02:43,535 --> 00:02:45,515
but the data ends in 2013.

70
00:02:46,255 --> 00:02:47,895
The right answer was empty,

71
00:02:48,055 --> 00:02:51,275
so broken SQL returning nothing looked correct.

72
00:02:51,895 --> 00:02:54,115
Now the tool rejects empty answers.

73
00:02:54,325 --> 00:02:55,185
Who looks first?

74
00:02:55,345 --> 00:02:57,765
Hiring managers for AI engineers.

75
00:02:58,445 --> 00:03:00,825
They read the report card, rerun it with one

76
00:03:00,825 --> 00:03:03,025
command, and open one mistake.

77
00:03:03,545 --> 00:03:06,200
It shows I test AI instead of trusting it.

78
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:08,200
The finished project will have one sample

79
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:10,720
database, about 50 test questions,

80
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:13,360
and Claude as the AI it tests.

81
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:16,460
It won't be a chat app, and it never changes the

82
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:16,920
data.

83
00:03:16,992 --> 00:03:18,792
The risk: I write the questions,

84
00:03:18,792 --> 00:03:20,792
so the test could be too easy,

85
00:03:20,792 --> 00:03:23,332
and Claude getting every answer right suggests

86
00:03:23,332 --> 00:03:24,312
it is.

87
00:03:24,772 --> 00:03:26,632
So I check every answer a second way,

88
00:03:26,632 --> 00:03:28,812
and next I'll add harder questions.

89
00:03:29,033 --> 00:03:30,073
Why this project?

90
00:03:30,573 --> 00:03:34,348
I already use SQL, Python and AI at my co-op.

91
00:03:34,853 --> 00:03:37,413
Testing AI and understanding why it fails is

92
00:03:37,413 --> 00:03:38,492
what I want to learn.

93
00:03:38,492 --> 00:03:41,132
The problem: AI can give wrong answers that look

94
00:03:41,132 --> 00:03:41,712
right.

95
00:03:42,392 --> 00:03:45,132
Ground Truth SQL tests the AI on your own data

96
00:03:45,132 --> 00:03:47,212
and shows what's wrong, and why.

97
00:03:47,752 --> 00:03:49,932
Today the checker works; Claude's only fails

98
00:03:49,932 --> 00:03:51,452
were my question's fault.

99
00:03:52,052 --> 00:03:53,852
Next: 50 harder questions.

100
00:03:54,492 --> 00:03:55,952
Running SQL is easy.

101
00:03:56,472 --> 00:03:57,572
Being right is the test.
